{"id": "EUVD-2026-103940", "enisaUuid": "3b36fc6c-ee67-3776-8704-367cb13b0623", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: discard post-EOF pagecache when extending a file via zero range\n\nsmb3_zero_range() removed the pagecache only for the range being zeroed,\nso when it extends the file the folio straddling the old EOF - which may\nhold data dirtied past EOF through an mmap - was never dropped and became\nvisible as file content once the file was extended.\n\nLower the discard boundary to the smaller of the zero-range offset and the\nold EOF.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3df27277f8f95345d4a6c57367824bf1aefdbf66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94949b6b2f2bf0dba2e8786aed0b08cc6bc3a183", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b75dadb50a25eed525264bf6fea44fad94e7626f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a8279c98ad289b27c0bdb11adb3f0c0b7fd456d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da4fe97fb6c730d9c94a115c7bfa6f98e0d578d0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98686", "GHSA-826x-h445-jqcg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0012f45b-dbf2-3170-bcb1-85bc7202002d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "0484f643-5e2c-35ee-a6aa-6dfff82e046f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "18eeef8c-b1d2-3b30-8d8a-97ee07f705d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <94949b6b2f2bf0dba2e8786aed0b08cc6bc3a183"}, {"id": "2d34bb1c-db16-3c5a-892c-151c9fdb29cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <da4fe97fb6c730d9c94a115c7bfa6f98e0d578d0"}, {"id": "35444450-2a1a-3c18-a389-6c3d5cf49827", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend